57 | Compensation: $6.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $527K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["OneMain Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.4B market cap on $4.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at -8.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 16.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (OMF) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Understanding_the_Setup:_OMF_and_Scalable_Risk_110226091602_1793672162.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793672162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"OMF Q3 deep dive: market questions credit improvement despite revenue growth and portfolio expansion","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/omf-q3-deep-dive-market-194136337.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793648496.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"JPMorgan Chase & Co. Issues Positive Forecast for OneMain (NYSE:OMF) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/jpmorgan-chase-co-issues-positive-forecast-for-onemain-nyseo